.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:69:      "summary": "com.apple.security.application-groups is now PROHIBITED on all four macOS targets and required on iOS only (new rule G4). The macOS credential transport question is closed: TASK-260728-7ii1xz selected the file-based system-domain keychain seeded over the NE app-message channel, with the non-secret snapshot travelling in providerConfiguration, and rejected the XPC candidate. None of the six grants the App Group entitlement actually confers on macOS is used by that design, so the capability has no current function on any macOS target and is withheld. Ceremony C1 no longer creates any App Group record or enables the App Groups capability on any macOS App ID. keychain-access-groups on macos.provider moves from prohibited-pending-decision to a settled prohibited, and loses the resolutionOwner and amendmentRule that existed only to keep it open; rule K1 replaces that amendmentRule with the correct, narrow reopening condition. OC-1 is closed; OC-4 is downgraded. Every accepted r2/r3 decision - the four production identifiers and their containment, channel-keyed Network Extension values, the registered iOS-style App Group literals, the legacy no-migration rule, the Sparkle Mach lookup exception and rule X1, profile classes, and C1's iOS exclusions - is preserved.",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:70:      "verifiedIndependently": "The finding was re-checked before being accepted, not taken on trust. The macOS App Group grant set was read directly out of /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb on macOS 26.5 (25F71): lines 302-330 and 459-465 are the only two places the entitlement appears, and they confer exactly six grants (recorded field-by-field in appGroupLeastPrivilegeRule.survey). Three are home-relative and therefore break across the root/user boundary; three are system-wide and are used by no candidate the transport decision kept. The claim that a root provider needs no keychain entitlement was likewise re-verified locally: application.sb:792-793 grants /Library/Keychains read+write to any com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension holder, and application.sb:655-656 grant the securityd/SecurityServer Mach lookups to every sandboxed process, exactly as TASK-260728-7ii1xz reported. CONFIRMED."
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:228:    "contingency": "OC-4"
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:236:    "evidence": "Observed 2026-07-28 on this Mac: Tailscale's and Surfshark's packet-tunnel system extensions both ship com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.absolute-path.read-write entries for /private/var/root/Library/Group Containers/, which is direct evidence that a root provider's group container is not the user's. The full grant survey behind the macOS verdict is in appGroupLeastPrivilegeRule.",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:375:          "rationale": "Withheld under least privilege (rule G4): no grant this entitlement confers on macOS is used by the selected design. The six grants were read out of the system App Sandbox profile rather than assumed - three are home-relative and break across the root/user boundary, three are system-wide and belong to mechanisms this project does not use (Mac App Store group content, a group-prefixed XPC Mach service, group-prefixed POSIX IPC). The host-to-provider channel selected by TASK-260728-7ii1xz is providerConfiguration plus a sendProviderMessage seed into a provider-owned system-domain keychain item, and its XPC candidate - the only one that would have needed a group-prefixed Mach name - was rejected. A private group container is redundant with the container every sandboxed target already gets unconditionally (application.sb:107-108).",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:376:          "evidence": "/System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb on macOS 26.5 (25F71): the entitlement appears at lines 302-330 and 459-465 and nowhere else. Full per-grant survey in appGroupLeastPrivilegeRule.survey.",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:397:          "verifyAtFirstBuild": "OC-2"
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:468:          "rationale": "Withheld under least privilege (rule G4): no grant this entitlement confers on macOS is used by the selected design. The six grants were read out of the system App Sandbox profile rather than assumed - three are home-relative and break across the root/user boundary, three are system-wide and belong to mechanisms this project does not use (Mac App Store group content, a group-prefixed XPC Mach service, group-prefixed POSIX IPC). The host-to-provider channel selected by TASK-260728-7ii1xz is providerConfiguration plus a sendProviderMessage seed into a provider-owned system-domain keychain item, and its XPC candidate - the only one that would have needed a group-prefixed Mach name - was rejected. A private group container is redundant with the container every sandboxed target already gets unconditionally (application.sb:107-108).",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:469:          "evidence": "/System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb on macOS 26.5 (25F71): the entitlement appears at lines 302-330 and 459-465 and nowhere else. Full per-grant survey in appGroupLeastPrivilegeRule.survey.",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:476:          "rationale": "Settled by TASK-260728-7ii1xz. The selected transport is the file-based system-domain keychain, whose access-control model is per-item SecAccess ACLs, not access groups (Apple TN3137: 'The file-based keychain uses access control lists (SecAccess). The data protection keychain uses keychain access groups.'). The entitlement is therefore INAPPLICABLE to the mechanism actually used, not merely unnecessary. The provider needs no keychain entitlement at all: application.sb:792-793 already grants /Library/Keychains read+write to any process holding com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension, and application.sb:655-656 grant the securityd/SecurityServer Mach lookups to every sandboxed process. No new entitlement, no new App ID, no new portal capability, no change to Ceremony C1.",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:477:          "evidence": "Observed 2026-07-28 on this Mac via codesign -d --entitlements :- on the installed system extensions: PureVPN's providers carry keychain-access-groups, Surfshark's carries a temporary-exception path for /Library/Keychains/. Both observations stand and neither is a requirement argument - see rule K1. Re-verified independently for r4 at /System/Library/Sandbox/Profiles/application.sb on macOS 26.5 (25F71): application.sb:792-793 (NE-entitled processes get /Library/Keychains read+write) and application.sb:655-656 (com.apple.securityd.xpc and com.apple.SecurityServer Mach lookups allowed unconditionally). Checks E8-E10 in TASK-260728-7ii1xz_macos-credential-transport-decision.md.",
.temp/resources/TASK-260715-ypo7yo/TASK-260715-ypo7yo_apple-identifier-entitlement-matrix.json:681:          "rationale": "Withheld under least privilege (rule G4): no grant this entitlement confers on macOS is used by the selected design. The six grants were read out of the system App Sandbox profile rather than assumed - three are home-relative and break across the root/user boundary, three are system-wide and belong to mechanisms this project does not use (Mac App Store group content, a group-prefixed XPC Mach service, group-prefixed POSIX IPC). The host-to-provider channel selected by TASK-260728-7ii1xz is providerConfiguration plus a sendProviderMessage seed into a provider-owned system-domain keychain item, and its XPC candidate - the only one that would have needed a group-prefixed Mach name - was rejected. A private group container is redundant with the container every sandboxed target already gets unconditionally (application.sb:107-108).",
